        "turno.contestoSintesiInvalida.perche": "The model in charge of summarizing the conversation answered in a form that cannot be verified: the summary text is missing, or the signal that says whether it finished is missing. The context discarded it instead of publishing it. {originali}",
        "turno.contestoSintesiInvalida.rimedio": "If it always happens with this model, change the summary model in Context Manager’s advanced settings: some models spend all the response space on reasoning and leave none for the summary.",
        "turno.contestoCitazioni.perche": "A summary is accepted only if it quotes pieces of the original messages word for word: it is the check that stops it from making things up. Here none of the proposed quotes was found in the originals of this conversation, and the summary was rejected. {originali}",
        "turno.contestoCitazioni.rimedio": "If it repeats, choose another model for the summary in Context Manager’s advanced settings: copying a quote word for word is the first thing smaller models get wrong.",
        "turno.contestoTroncata.perche": "The summary stopped before the end: the response space ran out before the model could close it. TALOS already asked a second time, shorter, and that one did not arrive whole either; it will not try again. {originali}",
